A||N||4||msweldon||Need some tech info on the 3.4 DOHC||||1||
Z||000000||msweldon||05-16-2001||04:38 PM||||I need the following specs for the 3.4 DOHC engine.  If anyone has them please let me know.<P>BLOCK: Chevy 209 3.4L<BR>Bore: 3.920 in<BR>Stroke: 3.310<BR>Intake Valve Diameter:<BR>Exhaust Valve Diameter:<BR>Compression Ratio:<BR>Induction Flow cfm:<BR>Manifold Type: SFI for 96' models<BR>Camshaft Lifter Type:<BR>Intake Camshaft Lift:<BR>Intake Camshaft Duration:<BR>Exh Camshaft Lift:<BR>Exh Camshaft Duration:<BR>Stock Timing:<P>Or if anyone has a complete Dyno2000 file for the DOHC please ship it my way.<P>Many thanks,<BR>Marc Weldon||||reg||1
Z||000001||87GTZ34||05-16-2001||05:38 PM||||Hey Marc, do you have a copy of dyno2000?  I can dig out some of the specs that you're looking for.<BR> <BR>BTW Is that the actual bore?  I think it should be 3.6228 and the stroke is 3.307 yielding 204 cubes or 3350 CCs<BR><p>[This message has been edited by 87GTZ34 (edited 05-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Will||05-16-2001||07:55 PM||||I'm pretty sure it uses flat tappet hydraulic lifters.<BR>I think the camshaft specs are in the service manual. Most of the rest of what you're looking for should be there, too. Probably not the CFM number, though.||||reg||1
Z||000003||88formula||05-16-2001||08:07 PM||||The actual displacement is 204.4 cubic inches but if you bore the motor out .030" it will become 207 cubic inches. The bore is 3.620 and the stroke is 3.310. I don't know the valve diameters for the DOHC motor but I think I remember the compression ratio was 9.5-1. The 95 ohv Camaro motor had SFI so I would imagine the DOHC engine also has SFI injection.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||87GTZ34||05-17-2001||01:21 AM||||Marc, As I mentioned above those are the actual bore & stroke as listed in the GM w body manuals.  88 is right on cube displacement of 204.4 (i dropped the decimal).  <P>Int valve dia.  1.437<BR>Exh valve dia.  1.262<BR>Int lift        0.370 in at 108 atdc<BR>Exh lift        0.370 in at 115 btdc<P>Will is right about the lifters and they are a pretty oddball size too.<BR>Duration & timing is not listed and my engine is already apart.  If you play with overlap on dyno you can't get too radical due to splay angle.<BR>There are a couple of other forum members currently working on dohc engine they may have some of the other #s.<BR>'96 compression is 9.5:1<P>I don't know th actual CFM for the '96 but I built a table based on VE/RPM for matching turbos to the eng.  If you have a target range of VE and RPM I can give the CFM.<P>Also in '96, the coolant direction was reversed for better control of intake charge temp.<P>I haven't really done too much on mine.  I did contact several valve train component producers that said they will work with me on finding better than OEM parts.  Also I need to get my butt on some of the w-body forums to check out archives.<P><BR>||||reg||1
